(I)--from अव् to protect--see सूर्य;
1: Br. II. २१. 4; २३. २६; २४. ३५; III. ५९. ३७; IV. 1. १३८; वा. ५०. ६०; Vi. II. 8. ११-12.
got a place among श्राद्धदेवस्;
2: M. १३. 1.
the श्राद्धदेव;
3: Ib. १५. ४३.
an आदित्य;
4: Ib. १७१. ५६.
in three forms, गयादित्य, उत्तरार्क, and दक्षिणार्क;
5: वा. १०६. ५७.
movements of the sun, detailed; मण्डल measurement of; rise at Samy- amana, mid-day at अमरावती, mid-night at सुषा, setting at विभावरी; other similar calculations; the movement in a मुहूर्त; movement for a day and a night; movement in दक्षिणायनम्; chariot of, limbs of the year; the seven horses are च्छन्दस्, गायत्री, त्रिष्टुब्, जगती, अनुष्टुब्, पङ्क्ती, बृहती and उष्णिक्; gives a list of sages, Gandharvas, Apsaras, नागस्, ग्रामणि and राक्षसस् with the sun in the six seasons; these go with the sun in his own wheel;
6: M. chh. १२४-6; वा. १००. २२२.
a marut- गण;
7: M. १७१. ५२.
standard of नाग in the तारकामय.
8: Ib. १७३. 9.

--a son of विश्रवस् and केशिनी;
1: भा. VII. 1. ४३; IV. 1. ३७; Br. III. 8. ४७; वा. ७०. ४१-8.
pleased शिव by his praises;
2: भा. X. ८८. १६.
afraid of मान्धात;
3: Ib. IX. 6. ३३.
heard of शीता's beauty and set up मारीच to display himself as a golden deer and entice राम away;
4: Ib. IX. १०. १०
resented Arjuna-Haihaya's action in ruining his camp by blocking a river and was overpowered by him in the presence of women and imprisoned in his capital माहिष्मती;
5: Ib. IX. १५. २१-2; Br. III. ३२. ५०; ६९. ३५-7.
pursued by the king of kites, compared to Indra being pursued by वीर;
6: भा. IV. १९. १६-17.
killed by राम;
7: Ib. VII. 1. ४४; १०. ३६; X. ४०. २०; Br. III. 8. ५४; M. १२. ५०; ४७. २४५; वा. ८८. १९७; ९४. ३५; ९८. ९२.
lost his king- dom through pride of power; desire for more territory.
8: भा. X. ७३. २०; XII. 3. ११.
Vanquished by वालि at पुष्कर, agreed to be his ally.
9: Br. III. 7. २४८-67.
A description of:
१०: Ib. III. 8. ४८-50.
Killed अनरण्य;
११: Ib. III. ६३. ७४; वा. ८८. ७५; Vi. IV. 3. १७; १५. 1.
also दशग्रीव; defeated by कार्तवीर्य and released at the request of Pulastya.
१२: M. ४३. ३७-9.
